erica and i ask that all of us really  take a moment and honor all of those  as we turn on these lights we want to  remind people  where we bend where we will go in the  future  and just remember that somebody's family  is appreciative of what we are doing as  a community  so with that i'm going to invite my good  colleague  commissioner gibson up to say a few  words as well  thank you commissioner kirkpatrick  this is the first official day of  remembrance  of those who have passed on as a  consequence of the  of the covid pandemic  there have been as was indicated just  here in las vegas the greater las vegas  area and clark county  2873 who have died  as a result of their exposure  there are some who may suggest it's too  soon to do a remembrance  but i disagree i suspect that the  families of those  who have died would disagree and i  believe they would like  us to remember their lost ones  do it in a meaningful way not forget  and most importantly band together and  commit ourselves to whatever it takes  to overcome the current issues that face  us  with the raging virus  that has the capacity to take lives  it would be wonderful to announce  finally we're  finally ready to put an end to the  pandemic  but that isn't the case and we all know  that and as a result we know that the  twenty  eight hundred seventy three residents  who passed  is only part of the count we would hope  that the account would not get a whole  lot bigger  but we know that there will be others  who will succumb  so it requires of us a commitment to do  our part  the vaccine offers an opportunity  to do our part we hope that people  across this community will take it  seriously and if they have  already thought not to at least rethink  things  and consider it in any case we're  continuing to apply the resources that  are available to us  to get the vaccine out as fast as as it  is  provided to us and we've done about all  we can do in that regard  so there will be here  um an opportunity 